<ref name="RTReviewRoundup">{{Cite web |last=Campbell |first=Christopher |date=July 8, 2025 |title=Superman First Reviews: A Fun Comic Book Movie with Old-School Charm That Promises a Bright Future for the New DCU |url=https://editorial.rottentomatoes.com/article/superman-first-reviews/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250708234112/https://editorial.rottentomatoes.com/article/superman-first-reviews/ |archive-date=July 8, 2025 |access-date=July 19, 2025 |website=[[Rotten Tomatoes]] |quote=Critics say David Corenswet and Rachel Brosnahan shine together in James Gunn's colorful, earnest, emotionally rich adaptation that returns to the roots of the iconic character and gives fans plenty of reasons to be excited about the future... The movie is being praised for Corenswet's performance, his chemistry with co-star Rachel Brosnahan (as Lois Lane), and the comic-book-y plot and colorful visuals. If there's any problem with the movie, though, it might be too overcrowded with characters and ideas.}}</ref>

<ref name="VarietyReviewWar">{{Cite web |last=Gleiberman |first=Owen |author-link=Owen Gleiberman |date=July 13, 2025 |title=How 'Superman' Inspired a Movie-Review War: When Is It Fair to Say That Too Much Fun Is No Fun at All? |url=https://variety.com/2025/film/columns/superman-the-trouble-with-superhero-reviews-david-corenswet-1236458968/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250713201959/https://variety.com/2025/film/columns/superman-the-trouble-with-superhero-reviews-david-corenswet-1236458968/ |archive-date=July 13, 2025 |access-date=July 19, 2025 |website=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]] |quote=...when I look at the divided reviews of ''Superman'', it's as if I'm taking in the response to two entirely different movies. One of them is a ripping good yarn, a brash, jaunty, clever, sweet, rooted-just-enough-in-the-real-world adventure that conjures some of the deadpan serial nuttiness of the Superman comics of the '60s and '70s. The other ''Superman'', the one that's gotten kicked in the blue-spandex shins, is too fast, too frenetic, too snarky, too overstuffed, too empty of soul and emotion and conviction.}}</ref>

